WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.970
BEAR: Let's make a little
nature's candle out of rocks.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.605
DANICA: Get some rocks?
- Yeah.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.873
DANICA: OK.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.108
BEAR (VOICEOVER): Danica
Patrick and I are in the heart

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.110
of the vast Utah desert.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.945
She doesn't know
it yet, but Danica

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:15.882
just found us something to eat.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.450
Oh!

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.251
Scorpion.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.186
BEAR: We got dinner.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.154
Ah, there you go.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.021
DANICA: Let's not eat it.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:22.989
No, I'm not-- no.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.524
BEAR: Look.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.826
That was totally what I was
hoping I didn't have to eat.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.428
Don't make me eat a scorpion.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.029
Oh God.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.431
BEAR: Look at this guy.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.967
Scorpions, they can kill you.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.034
Enough venom to kill you.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.603
So yeah, I mean,
what we could do

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.506
is actually go and
actually look for these.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.708
If we found that under there,
we try and turn over a few more,

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.943
see if we can find
a couple of extras,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.813
make a little scorpion kebab.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.481
You dispatch it.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.315
No.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.450
Oh, this doesn't make me happy.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.986
BEAR: It's fine, it's fine.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:56.756
Don't let him get
away once you go in.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.626
Done.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.795
OK, so that's one.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.663
Try and get a couple more.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.299
DANICA: It was difficult
to take the knife

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.835
and drive it into
the scorpion's head.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.004
But this is survival.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.574
And so you do what
you have to do.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.642
OK, scorpions.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.277
Let's find some more.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.779
BEAR (VOICEOVER): The
stinger of a scorpion's tail

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:23.683
it's full of neurotoxic venom
that can cause extreme pain

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.619
and, in some cases,
paralysis and death.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:30.523
However, when eaten, nearly
half their body is good protein.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.792
If we remove the
stinger and pincers

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.162
and grill it just right, it
just might taste like something

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.664
you'd want to eat.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.999
But we're going to need more
than one to keep us going.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.267
So we're going hunting.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.304
OK, no scorpion there.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.073
This is a perfect place
for finding scorpions,

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.144
all of this dried brush.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.079
But don't use your fingers.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.547
Use a stick or a blade.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.952
Here we go, Danica.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.286
DANICA: Got another scorpion?

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.056
BEAR: This is a more
substantial one here.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.624
DANICA: More meaty?

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.027
Oh, yeah.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.062
He's a little fatter.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.697
Yeah.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.799
Thing is, I've learned
about scorpions--

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.335
and for years, I always
used to eat them like this.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.603
What?

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.304
And they taste disgusting
because they're full of--

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.606
Oh!

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.741
--this yellow kind of weird
stuff and really pungent.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.076
It stays with you forever.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:27.714
But if you cook them and
you barbecue them up,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.282
then it's perfect.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:33.253
DANICA: Thank God for the
fire because that's going

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.090
to make the scorpion
taste just like char

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.994
instead of a scorpion.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.462
BEAR: Here's your one.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.263
Thanks.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:46.733
BEAR: Don't let it fall off.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.834
DANICA: Do you like to cook?

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.335
BEAR: Yeah, I do.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:52.171
I feel I'm really
disappointing you, really.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.373
We should be having nice rosé.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.440
And--

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.341
Oh, yeah.
BEAR: Instead you're getting--

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.809
DANICA: We should, but--

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.847
This is like a downgrade,
I do feel, for your life.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.816
So how do you keep so fit still?

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.084
I work out all the time.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:07.053
I mean, I work out
almost every day.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.422
And has that helped
you with injuries at all?

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.623
I think so.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.526
BEAR: And have you had
bad injuries from crashes?

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.627
No.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.763
That means you're a
very, very good driver.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.197
DANICA: [laughs] Well--

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.032
It's like, you know--

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.500
You read--

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.002
Never fight a man who
doesn't have a scratch on him.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.404
DANICA: It's true.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.040
[laughs] Did you feel it
was harder for you going

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:31.377
in as a girl to that
world, especially

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.879
when you went professional?

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.981
Well, I mean, I don't know
if I thought it was harder

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:38.051
as much as I just
ended up realizing

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.586
it was harder kind of thing.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:44.223
I mean, everything from racing
to listening to people say

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.427
things about you to bad
days on the racetrack

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.728
and how to deal with them.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.129
You come back to the
bus and I'd be like--

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.664
(CRYING)
Oh, God.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.599
Why?

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.499
36?

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.567
I'm so bad.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.568
You know?

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.236
And you would just
have these really

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:03.509
flooding moments of self-doubt
and insecurity and yeah.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.078
And so you--

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.746
If I'm here long enough
with this scorpion,

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.549
I think it's all going to be
charred and burned in here.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.117
BEAR: Should we go
for the scorpion then?

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.885
DANICA: No, I was just
hoping that would happen.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.720
Here we go.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:14.554
You ready?

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:16.089
DANICA: [laughs] No.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.826
[laughs] Oh, gross.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.060
OK.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.195
It can't be that bad, right?

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.663
You eat them raw, right?
- Go on.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.364
Come on.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.798
Come on, lead the way.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.200
I love it.
- (SHOUTING)

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.267
BEAR: You got to keep it down.
You got to finish.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.235
[laughs] Do it.
There you go.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:30.570
You got it.
You got it.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.408
I just ate a scorpion.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.612
Mm.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.180
You seem like
you're savoring it.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.615
Is this--
- Mm-hmm.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:43.383
No, it's pretty bad.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.551
I can hear you say, mm.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.452
You're like, mm.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.086
BEAR: Mm.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:50.523
[laughs] Good job.

